; Interprets: 3GPP TS 32.299
;; What TS 32.299's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order: clause 6's procedures, then clause 7.1's Diameter AVPs and
;; clause 7.2's 3GPP specific AVPs. The commands' information-element tables
;; of clauses 6.2 and 6.4 already state each member's category (OM, OC, M,
;; O), which no block restates. Rf's commands are printed once under 3, Ro's
;; once under 4.
;; A clause pointing at another document for a layout is an `element`; a
;; rule depending on an earlier message, the charging domain, the node, the
;; SIP signalling or the operator's configuration is `text-only`.


;; Clause 6's procedures: what an answer carries in the flows of clauses
;; 6.1.1 and 6.1.2 (Rf) and 6.3.3 to 6.3.5 (Ro), the answer's record or
;; request type that of the request it answers, held to a success's answer
;; where the step says nothing of an error's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-event-record-type
; AVP: Accounting-Record-Type
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 6.1.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The CDF returns Accounting-Answer message with Accounting-Record-Type AVP set to EVENT_RECORD to the Network Element in order to inform that charging information was received."
    values 1 if request/Accounting-Record-Type = EVENT_RECORD and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-session-record-type
; AVP: Accounting-Record-Type
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 6.1.2
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The CDF returns Accounting-Answer (ACA) message with Accounting-Record-Type set to START_RECORD to the Network Element"
    values 2 if request/Accounting-Record-Type = START_RECORD and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The CDF returns Accounting-Answer (ACA) message with Accounting-Record-Type set to INTERIM_RECORD to the Network Element."
    values 3 if request/Accounting-Record-Type = INTERIM_RECORD and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The CDF returns Accounting-Answer (ACA) message with Accounting-Record-Type set to STOP_RECORD to the Network Element."
    values 4 if request/Accounting-Record-Type = STOP_RECORD and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; The direct debiting answer authorizes the service; the refund's carries
;; "the related result code", whatever it is.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-iec-request-type
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 6.3.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The OCS returns CCA message with CC-Request-Type AVP set to EVENT_REQUEST to the Network Element in order to authorize the service execution"
    values 4 if request/CC-Request-Type = EVENT_REQUEST and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The Requested-Action AVP (RA) is set to REFUND-ACCOUNT."
"The OCS returns CCA message with CC-Request-Type AVP set to EVENT_REQUEST and the related result code."
    values 4 if request/CC-Request-Type = EVENT_REQUEST and request/Requested-Action = REFUND_ACCOUNT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-ecur-request-type
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 6.3.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Once the reservation has been made, the OCS returns CCA message with CC-Request-Type set to INITIAL_REQUEST to the Network Element in order to authorize the service execution"
    values 1 if request/CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The OCS acknowledges the reception of the CCR message by sending CCA message with CC-Request-Type AVP indicating TERMINATION_REQUEST"
    values 3 if request/CC-Request-Type = TERMINATION_REQUEST and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-scur-request-type
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 6.3.5
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Once the reservation has been made, the OCS returns CCA message with CC-Request-Type set to INITIAL_REQUEST to the Network Element in order to authorize the service execution"
    values 1 if request/CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"Once the deduction and reservation have been made, the OCS returns CCA message with CC-Request-Type set to UPDATE_REQUEST to the Network Element"
    values 2 if request/CC-Request-Type = UPDATE_REQUEST and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
"The OCS acknowledges the reception of the CCR message by sending CCA message with CC-Request-Type AVP indicating TERMINATION_REQUEST"
    values 3 if request/CC-Request-Type = TERMINATION_REQUEST and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


;; The client's configuration, which no message carries.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: quota-holding-time-absent
; AVP: Quota-Holding-Time
; Section: 6.5.1.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Alternatively, if this AVP is not present, a locally configurable default value in the client shall be used."
    text-only


;; RFC 4006's grouped AVP, its own members read through paths from it:
;; Restriction-Filter-Rule, Filter-Id and Redirect-Server beside
;; Final-Unit-Action.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: final-unit-indication-terminate
; AVP: Final-Unit-Indication
; Section: 6.5.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Final-Unit-Indication AVP with Final-Unit-Action TERMINATE does not include any other information."
    excludes Final-Unit-Action = TERMINATE and Restriction-Filter-Rule or Final-Unit-Action = TERMINATE and Filter-Id or Final-Unit-Action = TERMINATE and Redirect-Server


;; After an earlier CCA's final units are consumed.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: terminate-action-used-service-unit
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 6.5.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Network Element shall send CCR message with CC-Request-Type AVP set to the value UPDATE_REQUEST and report the Used-Service-Unit AVP for the service that has terminated, as defined in RFC 4006 [402]."
    text-only


;; A CCA's Multiple-Services-Credit-Control: a `default` within it would
;; hold to Offline-Charging's too, whose absent Quota-Consumption-Time is
;; the Offline-Charging AVP's own (clause 7.2.121).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: quota-consumption-time-absent
; AVP: Quota-Consumption-Time
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 6.5.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If a Quota-Consumption-Time AVP value of zero is provided, or if no Quota-Consumption-Time AVP is present in the CCA, the quota is consumed continuously from the point at which it is granted."
    text-only


;; The 3GPP features' lists: TS 29.229 clause 6.3.29 has a vendor's own
;; features carry its own Vendor-Id, and which list a Supported-Features
;; carries only its Vendor-Id and Feature-List-ID tell.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: supported-features-vendor
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Section: 6.5.10.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The value 10415 (3GPP) is used as Vendor-Id, and the Feature-List-ID and Feature-List are defined per middle tier TS."
    text-only


;; The initial request is read as an ACR[Start]: whether an ACR[Event] is one
;; the clause does not say. Whether the server supports the mechanism the
;; answer does not show. The request's Supported-Features, which the ACR's
;; ABNF leaves to its * [ AVP ], no rule reads: an answer with
;; DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED answers a request holding one.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-supported-features
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 6.5.10.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which does not include any Supported-Features AVP, the server shall include in the answer, if supported, Supported-Features AVPs identifying the complete set of features supported by the server for this domain / subsystem / service."
    text-only
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which includes the Supported-Features AVP, the server shall behave as follows:"
"If all features indicated in the Supported-Features AVP are supported, and the process for online or offline charging is successful, a successful answer with the Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS is returned and includes, if supported, Supported-Features AVPs identifying the complete set of features supported by the server for this domain / subsystem / service."
    text-only
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which includes the Supported-Features AVP, the server shall behave as follows:"
"If not all the features indicated in the Supported-Features AVP are supported, the answer is returned with Experimental-Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED and includes the Supported-Features AVPs containing lists of all features supported by the server."
    present-if Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415 and Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED and request/Accounting-Record-Type = START_RECORD


;; Whether the request held a Supported-Features, which the ACR's ABNF leaves
;; to its * [ AVP ], no rule reads; and a Failed-AVP holding it no path
;; reaches.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-supported-features-failed-avp
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 6.5.10.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which includes the Supported-Features AVP, the server shall behave as follows:"
"If Supported-Features AVP is not supported by the server, the answer is returned, as per 'M' bit set rule, with the Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_AVP_UNSUPPORTED and a Failed-AVP AVP containing at least one Supported-Features AVP as received in the request."
    text-only


;; The initial request is read as a CCR[Initial]: whether a CCR[Event] is one
;; the clause does not say. As the ACA's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-supported-features
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 6.5.10.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which does not include any Supported-Features AVP, the server shall include in the answer, if supported, Supported-Features AVPs identifying the complete set of features supported by the server for this domain / subsystem / service."
    text-only
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which includes the Supported-Features AVP, the server shall behave as follows:"
"If all features indicated in the Supported-Features AVP are supported, and the process for online or offline charging is successful, a successful answer with the Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_SUCCESS is returned and includes, if supported, Supported-Features AVPs identifying the complete set of features supported by the server for this domain / subsystem / service."
    text-only
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which includes the Supported-Features AVP, the server shall behave as follows:"
"If not all the features indicated in the Supported-Features AVP are supported, the answer is returned with Experimental-Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED and includes the Supported-Features AVPs containing lists of all features supported by the server."
    present-if Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415 and Experimental-Result/Experimental-Result-Code = DIAMETER_ERROR_FEATURE_UNSUPPORTED and request/CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST


;; As the ACA's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-supported-features-failed-avp
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 6.5.10.3
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Upon receiving any initial Ro or Rf request for a specific domain / subsystem / service, which includes the Supported-Features AVP, the server shall behave as follows:"
"If Supported-Features AVP is not supported by the server, the answer is returned, as per 'M' bit set rule, with the Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_AVP_UNSUPPORTED and a Failed-AVP AVP containing at least one Supported-Features AVP as received in the request."
    text-only


;; Rf's commands are RFC 6733's accounting application's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: acct-application-id-rf
; AVP: Acct-Application-Id
; Section: 7.1.5
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Acct-Application-Id AVP (AVP code 259) shall contain the value of 3 as defined in RFC 6733 [401] according TS 29.230 [206]."
    range 3


;; Ro's commands are RFC 4006's credit-control application's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: auth-application-id-ro
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Section: 7.1.6
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Auth-Application-Id AVP (AVP code 258) shall contain the value of 4 as defined in RFC 4006 [402] according TS 29.230 [206]."
    range 4


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: called-station-id-apn
; AVP: Called-Station-Id
; Section: 7.1.7
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Called-Station-Id AVP (AVP code 30) shall contain the Access Point Name (APN) the user is connected to."
    encoding apn


;; Of each answer printing Experimental-Result.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aca-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 7.1.8A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Vendor-ID AVP shall contain 3GPP (10415), and following values are used for Experimental-Result-Code:"
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-experimental-result-vendor
; AVP: Experimental-Result
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 7.1.8A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Vendor-ID AVP shall contain 3GPP (10415), and following values are used for Experimental-Result-Code:"
    requires Experimental-Result/Vendor-Id = 10415


;; DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED (5031), the answer's own Result-Code; the code a
;; Multiple-Services-Credit-Control carries for one rating group is the
;; group's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-rating-failed-failed-avp
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 7.1.11
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This error code is used to inform the CTF that the OCF cannot rate the service request due to insufficient rating input, incorrect AVP combination or due to an AVP or an AVP value that is not recognized or supported in the rating."
"The Failed-AVP AVP MUST be included and contain a copy of the entire AVP(s) that could not be processed successfully or an example of the missing AVP complete with the Vendor-Id if applicable."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED


;; A text's form, dot-separated parts and a domain: no codec reads it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: service-context-id-format
; AVP: Service-Context-Id
; Section: 7.1.12
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"As a minimum, \"Release\".\"service-context\" \"@\" \"domain\" shall be used."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: vendor-specific-application-id-vendor
; AVP: Vendor-Id
; Within: Vendor-Specific-Application-Id
; Section: 7.1.16
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Vendor-Id AVP (AVP code 266), as part of the grouped Vendor-Specific-Application-Id AVP, shall contain the value of 10415, which is the IANA registered value for '3GPP' in TS 29.230 [206]."
    range 10415


;; The charging domain decides the digits' form, which the AVP does not
;; carry, and digits as text where a sibling's value says IMEISV no kind
;; says.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-equipment-info-imeisv
; AVP: User-Equipment-Info
; Section: 7.1.17
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"For PS charging, when the User-Equipment-Info-Type AVP (AVP code 459) is set to IMEISV (0), the value within the User-Equipment-Info-Value AVP (AVP code 460) is of type OctetString and shall be a UTF-8 encoded hexadecimal."
    text-only
"For IMS charging, when the User-Equipment-Info-Type AVP (AVP code 459) is set to IMEISV (0), the value within the User-Equipment-Info-Value AVP (AVP code 460) is of type OctetString and shall be a UTF-8 encoded decimal."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: adaptations-default
; AVP: Adaptations
; Section: 7.2.4
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Adaptations AVP (AVP code 1217) is of type Enumerated and indicates whether the originator allows adaptation of the content (default Yes)."
    default Yes


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: address-domain-members
; AVP: Address-Domain
; Section: 7.2.8
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is present, at least one of the AVPs described within the grouping shall be included."
    members at-least-one Domain-Name 3GPP-IMSI-MCC-MNC


;; What a node uses, as TS 29.272's "is not used in S6a/S6d": not that it is
;; never sent, which `absent` would say.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: authorised-qos-not-used
; AVP: Authorised-QoS
; Section: 7.2.27
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This AVP is not used."
    text-only


;; "Either ... or" read as at least one of them.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: basic-service-code-members
; AVP: Basic-Service-Code
; Section: 7.2.29A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Either a Bearer-Service AVP or a Teleservice AVP is included."
    members at-least-one Bearer-Service Teleservice


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: bearer-capability-cap
; AVP: Bearer-Capability
; Section: 7.2.29B
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The value as described in TS 29.078 [233] shall be used."
    encoding element TS29.078 5.1 "BearerCapability"


;; SIP's header, which the message does not carry.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: called-asserted-identity-presence
; AVP: Called-Asserted-Identity
; Section: 7.2.31
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This field shall be present when the P-Asserted-Identity SIP header field is available in the SIP 2xx response."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: calling-party-address-unknown
; AVP: Calling-Party-Address
; Section: 7.2.33
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"In case no P-Asserted-Identity is known, this AVP list shall include one item with the value \"unknown\"."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: charging-per-ip-can-session-indicator-default
; AVP: Charging-Per-IP-CAN-Session-Indicator
; Section: 7.2.39B
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, that means charging per IP-CAN session is not active."
    default Inactive


;; The clause's heading and text name the AVP CSG--Indication.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: csg-membership-indication-default
; AVP: CSG-Membership-Indication
; Section: 7.2.46B
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this indication is not present, this means the UE is a Not member of the CSG cell for hybrid access mode."
    default "Not CSG member"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dynamic-address-flag-default
; AVP: Dynamic-Address-Flag
; Section: 7.2.57
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means that the address is statically allocated."
    default Static


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dynamic-address-flag-extension-default
; AVP: Dynamic-Address-Flag-Extension
; Section: 7.2.57A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means that the address is statically allocated."
    default Static


;; An envelope's state, and an order of the AVPs by their times: no kind says either.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: envelope-order
; AVP: Envelope
; Section: 7.2.59
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If an envelope has not been closed at the time of the usage report, then the Envelope-End-Time AVP shall be absent."
    text-only
"Multiple occurrences of this AVP shall be in chronological order, i.e. the first envelope is listed first in CCR."
    text-only


;; The initial CCA's, an earlier message for every later report.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: envelope-reporting-absent
; AVP: Envelope-Reporting
; Section: 7.2.61
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not included in the CCA[Initial] then the client shall not report the individual envelopes."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: forwarding-pending-default
; AVP: Forwarding-Pending
; Section: 7.2.67aA
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"When it is not present, the voice call is not expected to be forwarded."
    default "Forwarding not pending"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: inter-ue-transfer-default
; AVP: Inter-UE-Transfer
; Section: 7.2.74aA
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means that the type of transfer is Intra-UE transfer."
    default "Intra-UE transfer"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ims-emergency-indicator-default
; AVP: IMS-Emergency-Indicator
; Section: 7.2.76A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means the IMS session or registration is not detected as an emergency session or registration."
    default "Non Emergency"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: imsi-unauthenticated-flag-default
; AVP: IMSI-Unauthenticated-Flag
; Section: 7.2.78
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this flag is not present, this means the served IMSI is authenticated."
    default Authenticated


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: isup-location-number-tbcd
; AVP: ISUP-Location-Number
; Section: 7.2.80F
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It contains an E.164 number as transported in ISUP and is encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP does not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan; it contains only the TBCD-encoded digits of the address."
    encoding e164-tbcd


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: location-estimate-gad
; AVP: Location-Estimate
; Section: 7.2.94
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Refers to the geographical area description in TS 23.032 [227] for the internal structure and encoding of this AVP."
    encoding element TS23.032 7 "Geographical area description"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: media-initiator-flag-default
; AVP: Media-Initiator-Flag
; Section: 7.2.101
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The default value is '0' indicating the called party initiated the modification:"
    default "called party"


;; A text value: no kind says it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: message-body-sdp
; AVP: Content-Type
; Within: Message-Body
; Section: 7.2.103
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The message bodies shall not include the bodies' of Content-Type = \"application-sdp\" as these are captured in other AVPs."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: msc-address-tbcd
; AVP: MSC-Address
; Section: 7.2.111B
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It is encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP does not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan; it contains only the TBCD-encoded digits of the address."
    encoding e164-tbcd


;; Read through paths into the Offline-Charging's Multiple-Services-Credit-Control.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: offline-charging-time-mechanism
; AVP: Quota-Consumption-Time
; Within: Offline-Charging
; Section: 7.2.121
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"At most one of Quota-Consumption-Time AVP or Time-Quota-Mechanism AVP shall be present, if individual instances are not included within the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP."
    excludes Time-Quota-Mechanism and not Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Quota-Consumption-Time and not Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Time-Quota-Mechanism


;; That one of Quota-Consumption-Time and Time-Quota-Mechanism is there, not
;; both, no `members` form says.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: offline-charging-multiple-services-credit-control
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Within: Offline-Charging
; Section: 7.2.121
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVPs, if present, shall contain the Rating-Group AVP to identify the category, optionally one of Quota-Consumption-Time AVP and Time-Quota-Mechanism AVP, and optionally the Envelope-Reporting AVP."
    members at-least-one Rating-Group
    members only Rating-Group Quota-Consumption-Time Time-Quota-Mechanism Envelope-Reporting


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pdn-connection-charging-id-coding
; AVP: PDN-Connection-Charging-ID
; Section: 7.2.136
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Coding of this AVP is same as 3GPP-Charging-Id coding described in TS 29.061 [207]."
    encoding element TS29.061 16.4.7.2 "3GPP-Charging-Id"


;; A default of an IPv6 PDP-Address alone, which a `default` holding wherever
;; the AVP is read would give an IPv4 one too.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: pdp-address-prefix-length-default
; AVP: PDP-Address-Prefix-Length
; Section: 7.2.137A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The omission of this AVP for an IPv6 typed IP address implicitly means prefix length of 64 bits, as in this case the 64 bit prefix length default shall be assumed."
    text-only


;; PDP-Context-Type, a member of the CCR's PS-Information, whose own scope
;; does not see the CC-Request-Type; read through a path into the
;; Service-Information.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-pdp-context-type-initial
; AVP: Service-Information
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 7.2.138
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This AVP shall only be present in the CCR[Initial]."
    absent-if Service-Information/PS-Information/PDP-Context-Type and not CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ps-append-free-format-data-default
; AVP: PS-Append-Free-Format-Data
; Section: 7.2.155
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is absent or in value 'Overwrite', the P-GW shall overwrite all PS free format data already stored for the online charging session."
    default Overwrite


;; Quota-Holding-Time, a member of the CCR's Multiple-Services-Credit-Control,
;; read through a path into it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-quota-holding-time
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 7.2.160
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This optional AVP may only occur in a CCA command."
    absent-if Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Quota-Holding-Time


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: refund-information-ccr
; AVP: Refund-Information
; Section: 7.2.171
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This AVP shall be used by the CTF in case of a refund scenario and thus shall be included in the CCR for refund if previously received in CCA for IEC."
    text-only


;; Clause 7.2.236 defines no Trigger-Type value "indirect change condition":
;; the name is Change-Condition's 34 (clause 7.2.37).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: related-trigger-indirect
; AVP: Related-Trigger
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 7.2.171Ab
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This AVP is only included when the Trigger AVP contains a Trigger-Type AVP with value of \"indirect change condition\" which is applicable charging per IP can session for a multi-accessPDN connection."
    text-only


;; Clause 7.2.175, in each command, whose `* [ AVP ]` admits it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-command-level-acr
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Command: Accounting-Request
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall not be used at command level."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-command-level-aca
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Command: Accounting-Answer
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall not be used at command level."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-command-level-ccr
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall not be used at command level."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-command-level-cca
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall not be used at command level."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-command-level-rar
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall not be used at command level."
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-command-level-raa
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall not be used at command level."
    absent


;; In a Multiple-Services-Credit-Control: sent only beside the
;; Used-Service-Unit it gives the reason of, and none of the values one quota
;; type's report carries.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: reporting-reason-usage
; AVP: Reporting-Reason
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall always and shall only be sent when usage is being reported."
    requires Used-Service-Unit
"The values QHT, FINAL, VALIDITY_TIME, FORCED_REAUTHORISATION, RATING_CONDITION_CHANGE, UNUSED_QUOTA_TIMER apply for all quota types and are used directly in the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP, whereas the values THRESHOLD, QUOTA_EXHAUSTED and OTHER_QUOTA_TYPE apply to one particular quota type and shall occur only in the Used-Service-Units AVP."
    exclude 0, 3, 5


;; A usage report carries its reason, in the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
;; or in the Used-Service-Unit.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: used-service-unit-reporting-reason
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It shall always and shall only be sent when usage is being reported."
    requires Reporting-Reason or Used-Service-Unit/Reporting-Reason


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rating-condition-change-trigger
; AVP: Trigger
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 7.2.175
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"When the value RATING_CONDITION_CHANGE is used, the Trigger AVP shall also be included to indicate the specific events which caused the re-authorization request."
    present-if Reporting-Reason = RATING_CONDITION_CHANGE


;; Two AVPs' values differing: no kind says it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: requested-party-address-different
; AVP: Requested-Party-Address
; Section: 7.2.176
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This AVP is only present if different from the Called-Party-Address AVP."
    text-only


;; A NOTE, which states no requirement.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sdp-media-component-charging-id
; AVP: SDP-Media-Component
; Section: 7.2.180
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"NOTE: When populating the SDP-Media-Component, either the 3GPP-Charging-ID or the Access-Network-Charging-Identifier-Value should be present but not both."
    text-only


;; What an interface uses, as Authorised-QoS's "This AVP is not used": a
;; `; Within:` scope holds in Ro's commands and Rf's alike.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: service-information-subscription-id-rf
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Within: Service-Information
; Section: 7.2.192
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Subscription-Id AVP in Service-Information AVP is only used on the Rf interface."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sgw-change-default
; AVP: SGW-Change
; Section: 7.2.200
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means this ACR[Start] is not due to an inter serving node change."
    default ACR_Start_NOT_due_to_SGW_Change


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sm-device-trigger-indicator-default
; AVP: SM-Device-Trigger-Indicator
; Section: 7.2.205A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means the Short Message is not related to Device Trigger"
    default "Not DeviceTrigger"


;; The charged scenario, which the message does not carry.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sm-discharge-time-scenario
; AVP: SM-Discharge-Time
; Section: 7.2.206
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It is only used in scenarios in which the delivery of the Delivery-Report (more properly the Status-Report) is being charged."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sm-status-length
; AVP: SM-Status
; Section: 7.2.209
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The OctetString is of length 1 octet and contains status information about the delivery of an SM."
    length 1 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sm-user-data-header-coding
; AVP: SM-User-Data-Header
; Section: 7.2.210
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Encoding is as described in TS 23.040 [216]."
    encoding element TS23.040 9.2.3.24 "User-Data-Header"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: sm-service-type-request
; AVP: SM-Service-Type
; Within: SMS-Information
; Section: 7.2.213
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The SM-Service-Type AVP shall be present if the SM-Message-Type AVP has value 2, SM Service Request."
    present-if SM-Message-Type = "SM Service Request"


;; The AS's SIP response, which the message does not carry.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: status-as-code-presence
; AVP: Status-AS-Code
; Section: 7.2.215A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If AS responds SIP 200 OK, this AVP isn't present in Application-Server-Information AVP."
    text-only


;; As Authorised-QoS's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: subscriber-role-not-used
; AVP: Subscriber-Role
; Section: 7.2.218
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"This AVP is not used."
    text-only


;; What an absent AVP means, where that is no value.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: time-indicator-absent
; AVP: Time-Indicator
; Section: 7.2.226A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Absence of this field indicates that the announcement is to be played before the IMS session is allowed to continue."
    text-only


;; An order of the AVPs by the SIP signalling, and a text value standing for
;; a value the SIP request did not give: no kind says either.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: transit-ioi-list-order
; AVP: Transit-IOI-List
; Section: 7.2.233B
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"Multiple occurrences of this AVP shall be in chronological order, i.e. the value in the SIP request is listed first."
    text-only
"If only a value for the SIP response is available, the Transit-IOI-List for the SIP request shall be included with the value \"unknown\"."
    text-only


;; NOTEs, which state no requirement, on the values one Trigger holds.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: trigger-type-notes
; AVP: Trigger-Type
; Within: Trigger
; Section: 7.2.236
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"NOTE 1: This should not be used in conjunction with enumerated values 10 to 23."
    text-only
"NOTE 2: This should not be used in conjunction with enumerated values 30 to 36."
    text-only
"NOTE 3: The threshold and the granularity of threshold are operator configurable. This should not be used in conjunction with value 50."
    text-only


;; Whether the user enters the cell or leaves it is what the presence of
;; User-CSG-Information tells, so the sentence states no rule a message can
;; break.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-csg-trigger-user-csg-information
; AVP: User-CSG-Information
; Within: PS-Information
; Section: 7.2.236
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"When used in a CCR, at entry to a CSG cell, the User-CSG-Information AVP shall be provided with the event report."
    text-only
"When used in a CCR, at entry to a hybrid cell where the user is a member, the User-CSG-Information AVP shall be provided with the event report."
    text-only
"When used in a CCR, at entry to a hybrid cell where the user is not a member, the User-CSG-Information AVP shall be provided with the event report."
    text-only


;; A CCR reporting CHANGE_OF_UE_PRESENCE_IN_PRESENCE_REPORTING_AREA (73) in
;; any Multiple-Services-Credit-Control's Trigger carries the area's
;; identifier and status in the PS-Information, read through paths from the
;; command.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-pra-trigger-pra-information
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 7.2.236
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"When used in a CCR, the Presence-Reporting-Area-Identifier AVP and Presence-Reporting-Area-Status AVP shall be provided in the Presence-Reporting-Area-Information AVP with the event report."
    excludes Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Trigger/Trigger-Type = CHANGE_OF_UE_PRESENCE_IN_PRESENCE_REPORTING_AREA and not Service-Information/PS-Information/Presence-Reporting-Area-Information/Presence-Reporting-Area-Identifier or Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Trigger/Trigger-Type = CHANGE_OF_UE_PRESENCE_IN_PRESENCE_REPORTING_AREA and not Service-Information/PS-Information/Presence-Reporting-Area-Information/Presence-Reporting-Area-Status


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: uni-pdu-cp-only-flag-default
; AVP: UNI-PDU-CP-Only-Flag
; Section: 7.2.238A
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"If this AVP is not present, this means both user plane and control plane can be used in UNI for PDU transfer, i.e. S1-U and S11-U respectively from S-GW, when Control Plane CIoT EPS Optimization is enabled."
    default UNI-PDU-both-UP-CP


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: vlr-number-tbcd
; AVP: VLR-Number
; Section: 7.2.242B
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"It is encoded as a TBCD-string."
"This AVP does not include leading indicators for the nature of address and the numbering plan; it contains only the TBCD-encoded digits of the address."
    encoding e164-tbcd


;; A text's form chosen by a sibling's value, Variable-Part-Type's: no kind
;; says it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: variable-part-value-form
; AVP: Variable-Part-Value
; Within: Variable-Part
; Section: 7.2.242aD
; Table: 7.2.242aD.1
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"String of digits, which shall be announced as a single number, up to 10 digits."
"String of digits, which shall be announced as individual digits, up to 24 digits."
"A string of digits in the form HHMM."
"A string of digits in the form of YYYYMMDD."
"A string of digits in the form of AAAAAABB, where AAAAAA is the integral part and BB is the decimal part."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: wlan-operator-name-twan
; AVP: WLAN-Operator-Name
; Section: 7.2.252
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The WLAN-Operator-Name AVP (AVP code 1307) is of type UTF8String and holds the Name of the trusted or untrusted WLAN Operator, as specified in subclause 19. 8 of 3GPP TS 23.003 [224]."
    encoding element TS23.003 19.8 "TWAN Operator Name"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: nr-cgi-ncgi
; AVP: Nr-Cgi
; Section: 7.2.254
; Versions: 18.0.0..19.0.0
"The Nr-Cgi AVP (AVP code 1325) is of type UTF8String and includes NR Global Cell Identity, with the format as specified in clause 19.6A of TS 23.003 [224]."
    encoding element TS23.003 19.6A "NCGI"
